#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# A paint editor: canvas, toolbar, and a pointer that knows which it is on.
#
#     ./bin/etcs scripts/paint_editor.etcs
#
# Pick a colour or a nib from the bar along the bottom, then hold any key and
# move over the canvas to draw. The window's cross ends the session.
#
# AN ORCHESTRATION, WHICH IS WHY IT IS HERE. It spawns from three providers --
# RenderProvider for the device, surface and shapes, WindowProvider for the
# window and its input, PaintProvider for the document and the brush -- so it
# is a composition rather than any one provider's script. The parts it is made
# of live with the providers that own them (PaintProvider/scripts/), and this
# file does nothing but assemble them into a program.
#
# ── THE FRAMES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The whole design turns on there being more than one, and on nothing having
# to know that but the router:
#
#   stage    1280x800  the window's frame -- what the input channel speaks
#   canvas   1280x740 at (0,0)      the picture's frame
#   bar      1280x60  at (0,740)    the toolbar's frame
#   swatch   44x44    at (16,8)     in the BAR's frame, not the window's
#
# A pointer report arrives in the stage's frame and is handed to
# Drawable2D_::PickAt, which walks the same ordered child list the renderer
# draws with -- so what receives an event is what the user can actually see --
# and returns the deepest node under the point WITH the point already
# translated into that node's own space. The toolbar's swatches are laid out
# at (16,8), and that is exactly the coordinate a press on the first swatch
# arrives as. Nothing anywhere adds an offset; the descent already did.
#
# WHAT THAT BUYS, concretely: move the bar to the top by changing one
# SetPosition below and everything keeps working, because no swatch and no
# stroke was ever stated in window coordinates to begin with.
#
# ── THE PARTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   gpu      RenderProvider::Instance    the device
#   view     RenderProvider::Surface     the window's presentable surface
#   stage    CompositeDrawable2D         the root everything hangs from
#   canvas   CompositeDrawable2D         the drawing area, and a Surface
#   bar      CompositeDrawable2D         the toolbar's own frame
#   paper    PaintLayer                  the opaque sheet
#   ink      PaintLayer                  what strokes land on
#   doc      PaintDocument               the layer stack
#   brush    PaintTool                   radius and colour
#   sheet    PaintSurface                binds the document to the canvas
#   palette  PaintPalette                which node means which setting
#   input    PaintInput                  routing, and the stroke machine
#
# THE CANVAS IS A SURFACE because every Drawable2D is one (ontology/Surface.h
# and Drawable2D.h) -- so the document renders into a REGION of the window with
# the same call it used when it had the whole thing, and the toolbar is not
# something the picture has to be aware of.
#
# ── THREAD LEDGER -- four ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. this script's thread   main.ProduceEvents -> input.ConsumeRouted
#   2. detached thread        main.ProducePointer -> input.ConsumeRoutedPointer
#   3. pool worker            Surface.ProduceFrames    frame clock
#   4. detached thread        Surface.ConsumeFrames    walk, record, present

spawn RenderProvider::Instance gpu
gpu.Create()

spawn WindowProvider::Window main
main.Create(1280, 800, 'ETCS Paint')

main.spawn(RenderProvider::Surface view)
view.Create(@gpu)
view.Clear(0.13, 0.13, 0.15, 1.0)

# ── the tree ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

spawn RenderProvider::CompositeDrawable2D stage
stage.Create(1280, 800)
stage.SetPosition(0, 0)
stage.SetBackground(0.13, 0.13, 0.15, 1.0)

stage.spawn(RenderProvider::CompositeDrawable2D canvas)
canvas.Create(1280, 740)
canvas.SetPosition(0, 0)
canvas.SetOrder(1)
canvas.SetBackground(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)
# THE BUFFER IS THE PICTURE, not something derived from the tree: the brush
# writes into it from outside the walk, so a recompose must not clear it.
canvas.SetRetain(1)

stage.spawn(RenderProvider::CompositeDrawable2D bar)
bar.Create(1280, 60)
bar.SetPosition(0, 740)
bar.SetOrder(2)
bar.SetBackground(0.18, 0.18, 0.21, 1.0)

# ── the document ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Sized to the CANVAS, not the window. The picture is 1280x740 because that is
# how much of the screen is the picture, and a document that thought otherwise
# would be 60 pixels of paper hidden behind the toolbar.

spawn PaintProvider::PaintLayer paper
paper.Create(1280, 740)
paper.Clear(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintLayer ink
ink.Create(1280, 740)
ink.Clear(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintDocument doc
doc.Create(1280, 740, 'untitled')
doc.AddLayer(@paper)
doc.AddLayer(@ink)
doc.SetActiveLayer(@ink)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintTool brush
brush.SetRadius(8.0)
brush.SetColor(0.10, 0.10, 0.12, 1.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintSurface sheet
sheet.Create(@canvas)
sheet.AttachDocument(@doc)
sheet.Render()

# ── the toolbar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The palette is bound to the tool BEFORE the bar is populated, so a swatch is
# never registered against a palette that has nowhere to put it.

spawn PaintProvider::PaintPalette palette
palette.BindTool(@brush)

run PaintProvider/scripts/paint_toolbar.etcs bar=bar palette=palette

# ── input ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Three bindings, and each answers a different question: BindRoot says which
# frame the incoming coordinates are in, BindCanvas says which single node's
# frame is the picture's, and BindPalette says who to ask whether a press was
# a selection. Without the root this is the unrouted edge and the canvas is
# assumed to be the window, which is what paint_surface.etcs still wants.

spawn PaintProvider::PaintInput input
input.Create(@doc, @brush, @sheet)
input.BindRoot(@stage)
input.BindCanvas(@canvas)
input.BindPalette(@palette)
input.SetBrush(8.0, 0.10, 0.10, 0.12, 1.0)

# ── the frame edge ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Compose, not Draw: the tree is re-walked every tick, so a stroke stamped into
# the canvas and a swatch that has just been pressed both show up on the next
# frame without anything here asking for a redraw.
view.Compose(@stage)

detach RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs view=view
detach PaintProvider/scripts/paint_routed_pointer.etcs window=main input=input

# The pump AND the press channel. Returns when the window closes.
main.ProduceEvents() -> input.ConsumeRouted()

main.Close()

input.Delete()
palette.Delete()
sheet.Delete()
doc.Delete()
ink.Delete()
paper.Delete()
brush.Delete()
bar.Delete()
canvas.Delete()
stage.Delete()
view.Delete()
gpu.Delete()
main.Delete()
